On Saturday, June 29, 2019 at 8:28:56 AM UTC+1, Helpdesk wrote:
> On Fri, 2019-06-28 at 09:01 -0700, Stefan Siegert wrote:
> > Y_ij = B_ij * M_i + E_ij
> > M_i = A_i * Z + E_i
> > Z ~ N(0, Q)
> >  Each
> > Y_ij, M_i and Z are spatio-temporal processes modelled as GMRFs (say,
> > CAR in space and RW2 in time) with individual hyperparameters.
>
> I not understand this with Y_ij: you say its its space-time but still
> Y_ij = B_ij * M_i + E_ij ??
> --
> Håvard Rue
> Helpdesk
> he...@r-inla.org
>

Yes, Z is a spatio-temporal process.
Each M_i is a known affine transformation of the process Z, plus structured and unstructured noise E_i.
Each Y_ij is a known affine transformation of the process M_i, plus structured and unstructured noise E_ij.
I want to infer the latent Z from the various observed spatio-temporal data sets Y_ij.
Does that help?

